text1:
The Kazimierz class was the first spacecraft class accepted into service within the Polaris Treaty Alliance Exoatmospheric Forces.  Initially designed by Smok Sysdyne in a bid for a Domain navy contract, one that would end up yielding the Champion Class.  Considered too experimental, and with a notable lack of firepower, the design would never- // WARNING  -the revolt of the PTA, the design would be praised within the Exoatmospheric Forces.  Its unique repair drone microforges allow for rapid sorties to be conducted back to back.  These forges would soon be found in all PTA designs. //UNAUTHORIZED DATA STREAM DETECTED
// datastream resetting... 

Most captains see the Kazimierz as a flying death trap due to the lack of internal structure.  However in exchange for this lack of structural stability, the Kazimierz gains unparalleled repair ability which allows for all aspects of the hull to be repaired mid combat.  The internal repair drones consume a mountain of preformulated stock to repair the hull, resulting in the Kazimierz’s peak performance diminishing quickly within combat.  The lack of internal structure solves this issue by letting crews fit mountains of feedstock within the Kazimierz, lending surprising longevity within combat.  Enterprising captains can even increase the performance of the repair drones, as long as they also increase the available supply of feedstock

Designed during the Early Rebellion period, the PTA commissioned Smok Sysdyne to build a capable frontline spacecraft.  The results of Flicker Core experiments allowed for a locally producible variant of a phase skimmer device to be installed. With a large front-facing weapon roster, the Hyacinth was the tip of the Exoatmospheric Forces spear which drove the Domain out of PTA territory.- // UNAUTHORIZED DATA STREAM DETECTED
// datastream resetting…

Despite most captains' qualms with integrating a phase skimmer into a ship of this size, the integrated phase flicker is even more stable and easily repaired than a phase skimmer.  Curious Commonwealth technology aside, the Hyacinth is largely reliant on its heavy weapons and armor profile to keep threats away from its vulnerable rear.

I want that //REDACTED phase cloaking rat ripped from the abyss!  Kowalski! Pull that //REDACTED out now so he can be roasted over a fusion core!’- // UNAUTHORIZED DATA STREAM DETECTED
// datastream resetting…

The Sluagh is a delicate yet fearsome design.  Utilizing weakly acausal principles to overload enemy ships, the tech behind the Sluagh is claimed to be wholly of Commonwealth origin.  Closer inspection suggests it cannot be due to its similarities to TriTachyon designs.  The Sluagh is nonetheless a fast, agile destroyer easily capable of forcing phase ships out of phase and dealing significant damage to them before they can retreat.

Seeking a faster alternative to the Kazimierz which could lead patrol sorties, a new design request was put forth by the PTA-EF.  The bid was taken in stride by a newly founded shipwright, Aitvaras Orbitinis.  Numerous setbacks delayed the project, and while the design criteria was eventually met, the Kaukas never shook its moniker as the “invisible spacecraft”.- //UNAUTHORIZED DATA STREAM DETECTED
// datastream resetting... 

A fast cruiser best sent on flanking attacks, or to destroy harassing frigates.  Its lackluster weapons profile heavily limits its effectiveness against larger ships.  Its speed paired with the inbuilt repair drone microforges allows the Kaukas to survive all but the most intense pressure.

//WARNING -the defeat at Kaimas and destruction of the 5th Battlegroup, the PTA requested a new capital class spacecraft to replace the lost number of Conquest Class’ within the Exoatmospheric Forces.- //WARNING -long backlogs, Smok Sysdyne answered the request.- //WARNING -after Jadwiga and her companions, the design would soon be sent to all reaches of the Polaris Sector.- // UNAUTHORIZED DATA STREAM DETECTED
// datastream resetting... 

Heavy modular slabs of armor fitted with unique sets of nodes clutter the hull, able to project both a damper field and emp emitter.  With a brutal weapons profile, fighter pilots are advised to avoid the Jadwiga at all costs.  The Jadwiga’s strong engines mean that Frigate captains are also discouraged from getting too close, lest the Jadwiga’s emp emitter fry your entire ship.   Commonwealth shipwrights often remark that dual emitter-damper nodes were fitted onto the Kazimierz after the design was proven on the Jadwiga.
